  "runner_up_case": "The honest case for FALSE rests on what the file lacks rather than what it contains. Every item supporting a 2024 conviction for delitos contra la Hacienda Pública is secondary press: one reputable outlet (Al Jazeera) plus two low-credibility aggregators, all paraphrasing a court statement nobody on the team has actually read. The file contains no primary Spanish judicial record — no Audiencia Nacional sentencia or comunicado, no BOE publication of the conviction, no Tribunal Supremo ruling — and the site:boe.es search surfaced only Rato's 1996 appointment as minister, not any judgment. Two concrete failure modes remain live. (1) Conflation: Rato's firm, well-documented tax conviction dates from May 2018 (conformity, 4.5 years, fiscal years 2012–2013); the 20 December 2024 judgment could be a different case — e.g., the Bankia IPO case, charged as investment fraud rather than offences against the Treasury — with 'three offences against the Treasury' being a journalist's paraphrase, or the Treasury counts could be among those of which he was acquitted. (2) Non-finality: an Audiencia Nacional sentence of December 2024 would ordinarily be under casación before the Tribunal Supremo, and Q6 — whether any Hacienda Pública charge has since been dropped or he has been acquitted — is still open as of 2026-10-01; if the Supreme Court has annulled the conviction or acquitted him of the tax counts, the unqualified claim is materially wrong as presented. On the current record FALSE is unlikely, but it has not been excluded by primary evidence.",
